THIRD-PARTY DATA
----------------

This product mirrors third-party datasets into your own deployment, and can
export them as an offline bundle for an air-gapped install. Each source keeps its
own terms, and those terms travel with the data — a built bundle carries this
same wording as an ATTRIBUTION.md file inside it.

- NVD (NIST). This product uses data from the NVD API but is not endorsed or
  certified by the NVD. See https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/terms-of-use.
- OSV (osv.dev). The aggregated database is published under CC-BY-4.0.
  Attribution: OSV, https://osv.dev, and the upstream database named on each
  record. See https://github.com/google/osv.dev.
- endoflife.date. A community-maintained dataset, mirrored under its published
  API terms. See https://endoflife.date/docs/api.


Cryptographic notice
--------------------

This product uses cryptography. It does not implement its own primitives; it
uses the Go standard library and the golang.org/x/crypto packages. Distribution
and use may be subject to export control or import restrictions in some
jurisdictions.


